Vary two overused rhetorical constructions to reduce repetition fatigue

The "X is not Y. It is Z" antithesis and "None of this..." openers had
grown into the book's dominant stylistic fingerprint (29 and 14 instances
respectively, several clustered 2-3 to a single paragraph). Rewrote about
half of each, prioritizing every cluster, while leaving isolated uses of
both constructions alone since occasional use is a legitimate device.

Verified via full two-pass rebuild: all 70 TOC entries still resolve
correctly, no cross-references broken, no accidental text duplication
introduced by the edits (caught and fixed two such slips before this
commit). 292 pages, 53,165 words (was 293 pages, 53,212 words) -- the
small dip is consistent with tightening roughly 30 sentences, nothing more.

